--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. GRAPH SCHEMA (as built)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Nodes (4 types):
  face:N        label "Face"  attrs: node_id, label, component_id, face_index,
                plane_id, area_cm2, normal_x/y/z, centroid (3-list),
                vertex_count, triangle_count, interior_angles (list),
                convexity, is_base_candidate=False, is_articulation_point=False,
                mean_curvature=0.0, curve_type="planar"
  hole:N        label "Hole"  attrs: node_id, label, containing_face_id,
                area_cm2 (Newell), is_filled=False
  curved:N      label "CurvedPatch" attrs: node_id, label, component_id,
                triangle_count, curve_type (surface_type), area_cm2
  component:N   label "Component" attrs: node_id, label, component_id,
                face_count

Edges (10 types, one edge per node pair - nx.Graph):
  EDGE_ADJACENT     Face-Face real polygon edge; built from vertex->face map,
                    REQUIRES >=1 shared pair CONSECUTIVE in BOTH ordered
                    polygons (wrap-around allowed); attrs dihedral_angle_deg,
                    convexity, shared_edge_length, orientation (FWD/REV).
  VERTEX_TOUCH      Face-Face sharing >=1 vertex, no consecutive pair; attrs
                    shared_vertex, shared_vertex_count.
  COPLANAR          |n1.n2|>=cos(1deg) AND |off1-off2|<=1e-4*extent; normal_dot.
  SAME_ORIENTATION  canonical normals equal, NOT coplanar; normal_x/y/z.
  PARALLEL          |n1.n2|>=cos(1deg), offsets differ, canonical !=; normal_dot.
  PERPENDICULAR     |n1.n2|<=cos(89deg); normal_dot.
  CONTAINS          Face->Hole and Face->CurvedPatch (smallest face_index).
  EXTRUSION_ALIGNED Face-Face both in one extrusion structure; see section 5.
  COMPONENT_OF      CurvedPatch -> Component ONLY.
  HAS_BASE          Component -> Face, emitted for EVERY face.

Graph attrs: G.graph["has_warnings"], G.graph["components_detected"].

Precedence (documented in module docstring): physical (EDGE_ADJACENT,
VERTEX_TOUCH) > geometric; COPLANAR > SAME_ORIENTATION > PARALLEL >
PERPENDICULAR; EXTRUSION_ALIGNED replaces geometric relations on marked
pairs, never physical ones.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. EDGE_ADJACENT IMPLEMENTATION (L399-425)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- vertex_to_faces: rounded-6dp vertex tuple -> set of face ids.
- candidates: every face pair sharing >=1 vertex (sorted tuples).
- _find_shared_edge walks face a's polygon edges; a pair is EDGE_ADJACENT iff
  both endpoints appear in b's vertex map and are consecutive in b (either
  direction, wrap-around allowed).  Diagonal-only pairs fail -> VERTEX_TOUCH.
- dihedral = acos(clamped n1.n2) deg; convexity via _edge_convexity;
  shared_edge_length = span first..last shared vertex on a; orientation
  FORWARD when b traverses in a's direction.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. EXTRUSION_ALIGNED (L250-306, L463-466) - OUTCOME ON BOX
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Per component: plane families (plane_id groups).  A pair of families is
eligible when parallel (|n1.n2|>=cos(1deg)), distinct offsets, both
internally EDGE_ADJACENT-connected.  Side walls = faces EDGE_ADJACENT to a
face of each family AND perpendicular to it; require >=3 side walls with an
EDGE_ADJACENT cycle (nx.cycle_basis, longest wins).  marked = cycle + both
families; emit EXTRUSION_ALIGNED for every marked pair.

IMPORTANT FIX (this session): the initial version SKIPPED pairs that already
had an edge (G.has_edge -> continue), so a closed box emitted ZERO
EXTRUSION_ALIGNED edges (top/bottom already carried SAME_ORIENTATION).  The
pair loop now REMOVES an existing geometric relation (COPLANAR/
SAME_ORIENTATION/PARALLEL/PERPENDICULAR) and re-adds EXTRUSION_ALIGNED;
physical relations (EDGE_ADJACENT/VERTEX_TOUCH) are never replaced.

Box fixture (2x2x2 cube): EXTRUSION_ALIGNED = 3 edges:
  face:0-face:1 (top-bottom), face:2-face:4, face:3-face:5 (the three
  parallel non-adjacent pairs).  The 4 side-wall-per-face pairs correctly
  remain EDGE_ADJACENT (closed box: every side face physically touches both
  caps, physical wins).  extrusion_direction = [0,0,1].

Also fixed: the face->component COMPONENT_OF edge (L468) was removed.
In an undirected Graph one pair holds ONE edge; HAS_BASE (emitted for every
face) already occupies the face-component pair, so the COMPONENT_OF write
was silently overwritten dead code.  COMPONENT_OF is now CurvedPatch->
Component only; Face->Component membership rides HAS_BASE (documented).

